<!--
  WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1, wave 2 — the 8 invented natives ruled at
  WEEPING_STONES_DESIGN_SITTING_1 (2026-09-24, closed af3eaa622):
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/weeping_stones_fauna_roster_2026-09-24.md
  §2, rows RM_Sillik/RM_Mirrik/RM_Ssurr/RM_Tirbak/RM_Burrak/RM_Vhakk/
  RM_Vellak/RM_Kirruk. Every row is franchise-free RM_ tier per Q11a — no
  donor content, no Star Wars content; the canon herd (Dewback/Fanback/…)
  stays on the Utinni patch layer per WildAnimals_WeepingStones.xml.

  `RM_Murrin` (roster row 2g, the pool fish) is NOT authored here — it
  already exists as STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1's own def
  (RM_StockedPoolFauna.xml, this same mod) and the fauna roster explicitly
  carries it to FISH_BY_BIOME_1 rather than casting it in this sitting.

  Placeholder art only (marked, not a considered choice — same precedent as
  RM_StockedPoolFauna.xml): every row below reuses a vanilla Core body
  texture retinted, chosen for silhouette fit, not for the pun. Real art
  rides the art queue as of this wave
  (infrastructure/artpipe/pending/weepingstones2_<name>_{south,east,north}.json
  for fauna, bare `weepingstones2_<name>.json` for flora — filed after a
  done/_artsrc/registry sweep found nothing existing for any of these 19
  names 2026-09-24).

  Sound cues and vanilla texPaths below are all MEASURED against the
  installed game's Data/Core (and Data/Odyssey for Alligator), not guessed:
  Pawn_Rodent_*, Pawn_Spelopede_*, Pawn_Iguana_*, Pawn_Muffalo_*,
  Pawn_Warg_*, Pawn_Pinniped_* (Alligator's own, despite the group file's
  name), Pawn_Dromedary_*, Pawn_Chicken_*, and the four vanilla
  soundMelee*/soundEating families all read from the real race files they
  are borrowed from.

  Water truce (§4/§10 ruling 3): already built at the BIOME level via
  `RM_WaterTruceExtension` on RM_WeepingStones_Biome.xml (WATER_TRUCE_
  RETRIBUTION_1) — every wildAnimal on this def, native or donor, is
  already covered; no per-row wiring is owed for the truce.

  Flight law (CLAUDE.md "if it flies in the fiction, it flies in the
  game"): RM_Mirrik and RM_Kirruk both carry real MaxFlightTime/
  FlightCooldown + race flight fields. RM_Kirruk additionally reuses the
  vanilla Chicken flying flip-book (`Chicken_Flying_1..8`, a real shipped
  asset) so it has genuine flight animation from wave 2, not just the stat;
  RM_Mirrik ships with no flip-book frames, which the flight law explicitly
  says blocks nothing (flight ships plainer without them).

  specificMeatDef/leatherDef: specificMeatDef is left unset on every row so
  the engine's own DefGenerator implies a meat ThingDef from race.meatLabel,
  same as most vanilla animals — no new meat items authored. leatherDef
  points at existing vanilla leather defs picked for fit (Leather_Lizard for
  the reptile rows, Leather_Plain/Leather_Heavy for the mammal-shaped rows,
  Leather_Bird for the flier).

  Mechanisms: the roster rules every row's v1 mechanism load as "none
  blocking" — no new C# is owed this wave. The optional comp reuses it
  flags (RM_JobGiver_FilterFeedTerrain/RM_MapComponent_ShadeGrid for Sillik,
  RM_CompVerminBreeder for Mirrik, RM_CompTameSootheAura for Ssurr,
  RM_CompDungSeeder for Burrak's v2 dig-catch-basin) are NOT wired in this
  pass — flagged as follow-on behavior wiring, not silently dropped.
-->
